{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026053445bdc0750c1ff94b38","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Extremely valuable — footnote 23 gives the full Dea Dardanica epigraphic corpus:\n- Cult of Dea Dardanica confirmed with eight stone monuments:\n  - 5 votive monuments with inscriptions dedicated to the goddess (3 from Venden locality, 1 from village Smira/Smirë, 1 from Kuršumlijska Banja)\n  - 2 monuments iconographic-epigraphic (2 votive plates from Romula-Malva in Dacia, with relief representation of the goddess and inscription)\n  - 1 sculpture from Mediana\n- References: E. Dobruna-Salihu, Votivna ara Deae Dardanicae i beneficijarna postaja iz Vendenisa, VAMZ 3, s. XLV, Zagreb 2012, 218-219; I. Popović, Dea Dardanica u verskom i političkom programu Konstantina Velikog (probably), Зборник радова 6 (ур. М. Ристић), 2008, 31-43? Actually \"Æ× Æ ÆÐ¿ÀÉÆÏ¿ 6\" — this is garbled Cyrillic. It's likely \"Зборник радова 6\" or \"Ниш и Византија 6\"? The title in garbled Cyrillic: \"ÇÈ¿ÒÎ¿ÀÎËÆ ÆÔ¿ÈÎ¿ÀÎËÆ Ô¿ÈË¿ÀÎËÆæ ÇÃÁ¾ÆÀÒÆÏ¿ Ò¿ÃÎÉ¾¿\" — Dea Dardanica u verskom i političkom programu Konstantina Velikog. The journal \"Æ× Æ ÆÐ¿ÀÉÆÏ¿\" — Ниш и Византија is published as \"Niš and Byzantium\" — symposium. Actually the collection with editor M. Ristić... Hmm, \"ÍÃ. M. ¿ËÁÒÆÏ¿\" = (ур. М. Ристић). Niš and Byzantium volumes are edited by Miša Ristić (M. Ристић)! So it's Ниш и Византија 6 (Niš and Byzantium 6), 2008, 31-43. I. Popović, \"Dea Dardanica u verskom i političkom programu Konstantina Velikog\" — yes, that's Ниш и Византија VI, Niš 2008. Good.\n\nLet me quickly verify this via web search later.\n\nNow, let me get the Greek inscriptions. The monograph only gives English translations. I need:\n1. The Greek text of the Asclepius dedication: something like Ἀσκληπιῷ Σωτῆρι Ῥοιμέταλκος καὶ Φίλιππα ἡ γυνὴ αὐτοῦ εὐχαριστῶς (?) ἀνέστησαν / ἀνέθηκαν.\n2. Hygeia: Ὑγείᾳ Ῥοιμέταλκος ὁ διασημότατος καὶ Φιλιππα/Φίληπτος...\n3. Telesphoros group: Ἀσκληπιῷ Σωτῆρι Σίμ[...] ἱερεύς.\n\nThese should be in IM IV (Inscriptions de la Mésie Supérieure IV, Naissus) — numbers around IM 158-160? Let me search EDCS. EDCS has a search interface at manfredclauss.de. Let me try to query it via WebFetch. EDCS search URL format:\nhttps://www.manfredclauss.de/gb/index.html — search form. There's also the old interface: https://db.edcs.eu/epigr/epi.php?s_sprache=en&p_sort=... The query parameters: \nhttps://db.edcs.eu/epigr/epi_en.php?s_sprache=en&p_konkordanz=CIL&p_suche=...\n\nEDCS provides a \"free search\" (Freie Suche) with parameters. Known URL pattern:\nhttps://db.edcs.eu/epigr/epi.php?s_sprache=en&p_sort=ASC&p_personennamen=&p_ort=Mediana&p_inhalt=Asklep&p_provinz=&p_land=&p_region=&p_herkunft=&p_fundstelle=&p_zeitstellung=&p_konkordanz=&p_konkordanz_nr=&p_art=&p_literatur=&p_text=&p_sprache=...\n\nHmm, I'm not 100% sure of parameter names. Let me try the web reader or WebFetch on EDCS search. Alternatively use EDH (epigraphy.packhum.org) which has HD numbers and a good search API. EDH is now at https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/... EDH inscription URLs: https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/edhd/inspect/HD000123. There's also a JSON API: https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/data/api/inscriptions/search?...\n\nLet me also try searching via WebSearch for \"Roimetalkes Mediana inscription\" etc.\n\nAlso I should check pandektis or the IGIQR... Let me start with web searches. Also search for IM Naissus numbers.\n\nPlan of searches:\n1. \"Roimetalkes Mediana Asklepios\" / \"Ῥοιμέταλκος Μεδιάνα\"\n2. \"IM IV Naissus 158\" or \"Inscriptions de la Mesie Superieure IV Naissus Asclepius\"\n3. EDCS direct query.\n4. \"Dea Dardanica Popović 2008\"\n5. \"bronze railing Mediana inscription\" — any inscription on the railing? The task asks about natpisi na bronzanoj ogradi — probably none are readable (I should say that honestly).\n\nLet me also check the Starinar 61/2011 (milosevic_iskopi.txt) — the ap11 files are Zotovic-Petrovic 1969. And the stibadium.txt. Let me grep for \"w-4\" in milosevic_vila.txt to get the 1971 excavation context.\n\nLet me do these greps in parallel with web searches.","signature":"dde10e004f4b468fa632deeb"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2e61857-1b3e-4231-a8c6-156332514500","uuid":"ae15a476-3039-479b-a380-c6ae8c482a50","timestamp":"2026-10-25T21:35:15.400Z"}
