tatuette pedestals — the \"Servandus\" votive? there's known votive inscription to Jupiter from Mediana?).\n- Also the frog with ZO[HN] inscription; ob dedicationem domus inscription; Aurelius Ampelius tribunus Batavorum inscription (CIL III ...?); southern church inscription.\n\nAgent D is overloaded; maybe split: D = bronzana ograda/herme; E = ostali latinski natpisi sa Medijane (Ampelius, ob dedicationem domus, ZO[HN] frog, altars). That's 5 agents — within medium guideline (≤15). Good.\n\nEach agent: report in Serbian, with URLs and confidence, mark conflicts. Tell them explicitly: DO NOT try to read local pdf files under medijana_baza/pdf (permission denied); use web only.\n\nAlso tell them the current date is 2026-10-25, prefer primary sources (EDCS, EDH, LSA, museum pages, academic repositories like rai.ai.ac.rs, Academia, journals).\n\nThen, while they run, I'll probe EDH/EDCS myself for Naissus to be able to verify/cross-check agent claims.\n\nLet me write the agent prompts carefully.\n\nCommon context block (I'll repeat in each prompt):\n- Project: Mediana (Naissus/Niš) 4th c. imperial villa, database for 3D reconstruction.\n- Task: epigraphic research; report facts with source URLs and confidence (visoko/srednje/nisko).\n- Known from local monograph (M. Milošević, Mediana — monograph 2011, English text extracted): porphyry statues inv. 985/R (Asclepius, 43 cm) and 986/R (Hygieia, 49 cm), found 1971 in room w-4, Greek dedications by \"Roimetalkes, diasemotatos\" and his wife; group Asclepius+Telesphoros on pedestal with Greek inscription of \"priest Sim[...]\".\n- Today's date: 2026-10-25.\n- Use WebSearch and WebFetch; try EDCS (manfredclauss.de), EDH (edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de), LSA (laststatues.classics.ox.ac.uk), IM references, rai.ai.ac.rs (Institute of Archaeology Belgrade repository), doiserbia.nb.rs, starinar journal.\n- Don't read files under medijana_baza/pdf (no permission); web only.\n- Report format: structured, in Serbian (Latin script), each claim with URL + confidence.\n\nAgent A prompt (CIL III corpus):\nGoal: inventory of inscriptions from Naissus and Mediana in CIL III / EDCS / EDH / IM.\n- CIL III: Naissus inscriptions are around CIL III 8197ff (also CIL III p. 232, 1030?). Find actual numbers and texts (at least the most important 5-10).\n- Search EDCS for \"Naissus\" findspot; EDH: place \"Naissus\" (HD numbers).\n- IM (Inscriptions de la Mésie Supérieure / Inschriften aus der oberen Moesia): Mirković volumes; Naissus IM numbers.\n- Deliver: table-like list: reference (CIL/IM/AE/HD), type, short text or summary, findspot, where kept now, URL(s), confidence.\n- Note conflicts between sources.\n\nAgent B prompt (Roimetalkos): as above. Emphasize: find the exact Greek text — try searching \"Ροιμητάλκης\" \"Μεδιανα\" \"Asclepius\" \"Hygieia\" porphyry; LSA entries for Mediana; Gavrilović & Vitas papers; M. Vasić \"Mediana\" ; also \"diasemotatos\" (διασημότατος) — honorific title; wife's name (maybe \"S[…]e\"? unknown — find). Also the Telesphoros group dedication with priest Sim[...] — full name? Published where? Also name etymology: Rhoimetalkes/Роиметалк — Thracian royal name (Rhoemetalces), \"Rhoimetalkes\" from Thracian *rhoimes \"ford\"? Actually etymology uncertain — have agent check (Detschew, Die thrakischen Sprachreste). Also note: was the dedicator a Gets/Thracian noble? \"diasemotatos\" = most illustrious.\n\nAgent C prompt (Dea Dardanica): statue from Mediana entrance, ~330; find: museum inventory (Narodni muzej Niš), publications (M. Vasić? Vujović? Gavrilović?), iconography parallels (Tyche/Fortuna of Dardania?), other attestations of Dea Dardanica (epigraphic? there are dedications \"Dea Dardanica\"?). Where is the sculpture today — Narodni muzej Niš or on site?\n\nAgent D prompt (bronze fence + herms): cancelli with herms, found 2000 ~250 m NW of villa with peristil; busts Asklepijos and Luna (Hygieia, Sol missing); chronology made before 325, installed 361 (Julian in Naissus), 