{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026060201f4831db826924041","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"WebSearch is denied. I have WebFetch and mcp__web_reader__webReader available. I can use search engines via WebFetch perhaps — e.g., fetch Google search results? That might be blocked. Let me try WebFetch on specific URLs:\n\n1. The RAI handle page: https://rai.ai.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1555\n2. EDCS search: https://manfredclauss.de/gb/grau.html — search interface is a POST form. Hmm. But there might be a way: EDCS has a search URL. Let me think about how EDCS search works. The EDCS website: https://manfredclauss.de/gb/griechisch.html ... Actually the search page is https://manfredclauss.de/gb/grau.html with POST parameters. Some people use GET: https://manfredclauss.de/gb/grau.cgi? Such as \"http://www.manfredclauss.de/gb/grau.html? Suche...\" Not sure.\n\nAlternative: use https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/inschrift/suche — EDH search has GET parameters like https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/inschrift/suche?&hd_nr=&....&tm_nr=&... The EDH search interface uses GET: e.g. https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/inschrift/suche?&lang=de&suchformular=erweiterte-suche&hd_nr=&ort=&fundstelle=&inscription_datierung=&literatur=&inschrift=&thema=&tn=&_format=... Let me try. Actually EDH advanced search URL format:\nhttps://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/inschrift/suche?&hd_nr=&tm_nr=&inschrift=Dardanica&...\n\nI recall EDH search: https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/inschrift/suche?suchformular=erweiterte-suche&inschrift=Dardanica\n\nAlso, EDH has a simple search: https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/inschrift/suche?search_word=Dardanica\n\nLet me just try fetching and see.\n\nAlso can use Google via WebFetch: https://www.google.com/search?q=... — often blocked by Google. Could try Bing: https://www.bing.com/search?q=... often works. Or DuckDuckGo html: https://html.duckduckgo.com/html/?q=... That often works with WebFetch.\n\nAlso MCP web_reader can fetch URLs.\n\nPlan:\n- Fetch RAI handle page for Milošević paper.\n- Use DuckDuckGo HTML search via WebFetch for \"Dea Dardanica\" Medijana, etc.\n- Search EDCS via their search engine. EDCS search page: https://manfredclauss.de/gb/grau.html. The actual search submission: POST to https://manfredclauss.de/gb/grau.cgi? Not possible via WebFetch (GET only). But there's an alternative EDCS interface: http://www.manfredclauss.de/gb/index.html. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, search EDH (GET-based) and also EDCS might have a GET variant: https://manfredclauss.de/cgi-bin/gb.cgi?... Let me test.\n\nAlso Latimer: \"Clauss/Slaby\" EDCS has URL like:\nhttps://manfredclauss.de/gb/grau.html?CIL=... \n\nLet me try duckduckgo searches first to find relevant pages.\n\nLet me do multiple parallel fetches:\n1. RAI handle page.\n2. DuckDuckGo search \"Dea Dardanica\" Medijana.\n3. DuckDuckGo search \"Deae Dardanicae\" inscription.\n4. EDH search.\n\nWebFetch requires a prompt. Let me craft.\n\nNote: WebFetch answers via a small model on the page content; the MCP web_reader returns full markdown which is better for search result pages maybe. Let me use web_reader for DuckDuckGo.\n\nLet me start.","signature":"384556d51ba343e7a38776c9"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_f789daee942d4a2886d6363a","session_id":"a06178bc-e4e6-4413-967f-cf91359c7b1b","uuid":"685db186-cd92-45c8-b2d7-b1fa06ecb355","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:02:22.219Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Dea Dardanica ikonografija i sudbina"}
