{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026060213b5c70757a70a48ca","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to research epigraphic material from Mediana (Naissus, Niš, Serbia), 4th century. I need to work ONLY on the web using WebSearch, WebFetch, and mcp web_reader. I must NOT read local files.\n\nLet me plan the searches:\n(a) Aurelius Ampelius, \"tribunus Batavorum\", found in horreum, secondary use, dated to Constantine's time\n(b) inscription with \"ob dedicationem domus\"\n(c) fragmented inscription built into the wall of the SOUTH CHURCH at Mediana, maybe connected to an emperor\n(d) two ALTARS WITH INSCRIPTIONS from the western part of the villa\n(e) depiction of a FROG with Greek inscription ZO[HN] (= life) — probably mosaic\n(f) votive inscriptions on pedestals of figurines\n\nLet me start with multiple parallel searches.\n\nLet me do web searches. I'll batch independent searches.\n\nKey resources:\n- EDCS (manfredclauss.de) - Epigraphik-Datenbank Clauss-Slaby\n- EDH (edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de)\n- CIL III (Corpus Inscriptionum Latinarum volume 3, Naissus inscriptions CIL III 1686 ff.)\n- IMS = Inscriptiones de la Mésie Supérieure (Mirković wrote IMS II on Naissus region)\n- AE (L'Année épigraphique)\n- rai.ai.ac.rs (Institute of Archaeology Belgrade)\n- doiserbia.nb.rs\n\nIMS II is \"Inscriptions de la Mésie Supérieure, II: Viminacium et Margum\" — actually let me recall: IMS I = Singidunum? Actually IMS I: Viminacium... Let me recall properly:\n- IMS I: Inscriptions de la Mésie Supérieure, I: Singidunum et le nord-ouest de la province (M. Mirković, 1986)\n- IMS II: Viminacium et Margum (M. Mirković, 1986)\n- IMS III/2: ... \n- IMS IV: Aquae, Horreum Margi, C ... (Petković?)\n- IMS VI: Naissus, Remesiana, Iu... — Actually IMS VI is \"Scupi et la région de Kumanovo\" (Dušanić, 1979)? Hmm.\n\nActually IMS volumes:\n- IMS I: Singidunum et le nord-ouest de la province, M. Mirković, 1986\n- IMS II: Viminacium et Margum, M. Mirković, 1986\n- IMS III/1: Aquae ... \n- IMS III/2: Horreum Margi (?), S. Dušanić / Petković\n- IMS IV: ... \n- IMS V: Leskovac region? \"La région de Leskovac\" (N. Vulić?)\n- IMS VI: Scupi et la région de Kumanovo, S. Dušanić, N. Vulić, B. Dragojević-Josifovska, 1979\n\nFor Naissus, inscriptions are mostly CIL III 1686-1690 area. CIL III has Naissus numbers around 1686-1700. E.g., CIL III 1686 = Naissus. The famous inscriptions from Naissus include CIL III 8247 etc. (additions).\n\nLet me just search.\n\nFor the frog with Greek inscription — Mediana mosaics. There's a mosaic at Mediana with a frog? Hmm. Actually there might be a mosaic with a frog and inscription. Let me search.\n\nLet me begin with a batch of searches.","signature":"deb4de1db0f345b8bdd7d594"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_83f9a667b513468bbb430a9a","session_id":"a06178bc-e4e6-4413-967f-cf91359c7b1b","uuid":"16adac12-2228-4f93-983e-e8acbb17f58d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:02:30.402Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Ostali latinski natpisi Medijane"}
