{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026060336732b80e839ef4105","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_e09a1f26218b4391b1ef6046","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Retry web_reader until success","prompt":"You have access to mcp__web_reader__webReader (a web page fetcher). Other web tools (WebFetch, WebSearch, Bash) are PERMISSION-DENIED for you — do not use them, do not attempt workarounds.\n\nThe web_reader tool is currently returning rate-limit errors (HTTP 429, code 1302). Your job: patiently retry until it succeeds.\n\nTask: fetch these URLs, ONE AT A TIME, in this order, using mcp__web_reader__webReader with return_format \"text\" and retain_images false:\n\n1. https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/data/api/search?find_location=Naissus\n2. https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/data/api/search?find_location=Mediana\n3. https://manfredclauss.de/gb/search.html (just to check if a GET search is possible)\n\nFor each URL: if you get a 429 rate-limit error, wait by making the next retry call (each call takes a few seconds of wall time anyway); retry up to 15 times per URL. If you get a 500/network error, also retry. If a URL succeeds, save the FULL text content returned (do not truncate it, but you may summarize if over 2000 words) and move to the next URL.\n\nIf after all retries everything still fails, report exactly that.\n\nYour final message: for each URL, either the full successful content or \"FAILED after N retries\". No other commentary.","run_in_background":false,"subagent_type":"general-purpose"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_b0d4e2e5af4a4f86b1e2d808","session_id":"a06178bc-e4e6-4413-967f-cf91359c7b1b","uuid":"d19c0b89-60f2-4c36-810d-6fe6518f54c3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:03:59.020Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"CIL III Naissus/Mediana korpus"}
