{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026060623afb4533bd9ed48ed","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still rate limited. Maybe the MCP server is per-minute limited. Let me wait a bit more, then try a simple, single URL (not a search engine — maybe search engines get blocked). Let me wait 120s.\n\nActually, wait — maybe the rate limit is from the MCP provider (Z.ai built-in tool) and there's a shared quota. Let me be patient: wait 120s, then try one fetch of a known relevant page, e.g., doiserbia search.\n\nAlternatively, is there a Bash-based way to fetch the web? That would be \"curl\" — the environment may have network access. The user said \"Radi SAMO na webu (WebSearch, WebFetch, mcp web_reader). NE čitaj lokalne fajlove\". Using curl via Bash is a web action but might be seen as working around denial. Hmm — the permission denial for WebSearch/WebFetch came from the permission system. Using Bash curl could be considered bypassing the intent behind the denial. The instruction says I should not attempt to bypass in malicious ways, but reasonable workarounds using other tools are acceptable (\"e.g. using head instead of cat\"). However, curl would bypass the permission system's network controls entirely — I'd say that's closer to bypassing the denial's intent. The denial explicitly says \"you *may* attempt to accomplish this action using other tools that might naturally be used\" — a natural alternative for fetching a URL could be the MCP web_reader, which IS allowed (no denial). So the allowed path is web_reader only.\n\nLet me be patient with web_reader rate limits. Let me wait 120-180 s between calls, and prioritize the most valuable URLs.\n\nPlan of fetches (in priority order), each spaced:\n1. doiserbia.nb.rs search for \"Mediana\" bronze — actually doiserbia has a search: https://doiserbia.nb.rs/ with a query param? The search URL format: https://doiserbia.nb.rs/Article.aspx?id=... Need to find articles. Alternatively use Google Scholar via web_reader — might be blocked.\n\nLet me think about what I know from prior knowledge to guide fetches:\n- The Mediana bronze railing with herms was published by... I recall a paper by Ivan Popović / Mihailo Vujović about \"Bronze furniture from Mediana\". Also \"Gavrilović, N.\" wrote about \"Bronze lamp from Mediana\"? Actually Nadežda Gavrilović wrote on Mediana mosaics? Vujović wrote \"Mediana: residence of tetrarchs\" etc.\n- There's a known article: M. Vasić, \"Mediana\" and Ivan Popović \"Hristijanski konsep...\" Hmm.\n- There is a known paper: I. Popović, \"Bronzana ograda iz Medijane\"? Not sure.\n- Also the 2000 excavation was led by Miroslav Vasić? Or by Ksenija? The rescue excavations at Mediana in 2000 were directed by M. Vasić (Archaeological Institute). The bronze railing/ostava was published by Ivan Popović in \"Starinar\" maybe: \"Bronze railing from Mediana\" Starinar LII (2002)? Hmm.\n\nBetter to actually fetch. Let me use web_reader with spaced attempts.\n\nCandidate URLs:\n- https://doiserbia.nb.rs/Article.aspx?ref=0350-0241... unknown.\n- Search via doiserbia: https://doiserbia.nb.rs/SearchResults.aspx?query=... unknown param names.\n- rai.ai.ac.rs — Archaeological Institute repository? Actually rai.ai.ac.rs is \"Republička agencija...\"? Hmm, rai.ai.ac.rs = \"Repozitorijum Arheološkog instituta\" (ai.ac.rs is the Archaeological Institute Belgrade domain; rai = repozitorijum AI). It likely has OAI-PMH or a browse interface.\n\nLet me wait and then fetch ai.ac.rs repository search.\n\nI'll wait 120s.","signature":"4d42879faed244aea0bb03a4"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_2efeac14a2c7412497732372","session_id":"a06178bc-e4e6-4413-967f-cf91359c7b1b","uuid":"5975a6d6-2128-4bf3-a956-194fba0fdcd3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:06:46.307Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Bronzana ograda herme natpisi"}
