{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026102606101034ee9b83031e4371","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The web reader is persistently rate-limited. Total elapsed since session start: roughly 15+ minutes, ~70 attempts, only 2 successes (one real: the manfredclauss search page HTML at the very beginning, which I didn't get to see the content of because... wait, actually the first successful call — I never saw its content because the tool result shows only \"Successfully fetched and processed URL...\" — the content was delivered to the harness but the result text shown to me was truncated to that line. Hmm, actually the result of that call was just the message; the content presumably was available but the displayed output was that string. So I never got the content.\n\nAt this point I must write the honest report. I cannot verify ANY numbers online. Per instructions, I must not invent numbers.\n\nHowever, I can still provide substantial value: I can lay out the corpora structure (what's known about them bibliographically), the anchor points that the caller themselves provided, and a concrete retrieval plan. And I can list the handful of Naissus/Mediana inscriptions that are so well attested in general literature that I can state them with a confidence label — but only those where I'm genuinely confident of content even if not of exact numbers. The instruction: \"Ako nešto ne možeš da potvrdiš ... reci to iskreno — ne izmišljaj brojeve.\"\n\nKnown-with-confidence facts about Naissus epigraphy that are general knowledge (not numbers):\n- The imperial city of Naissus: birthplace of Constantine; in 4th century Constantius Chlorus' palace; Mediana as suburban imperial residence.\n- Inscriptions found at Mediana include honorific/dedication inscriptions to emperors (e.g., a dedication to Constantius Chlorus/Galerius?), and the famous inscription mentioning \"Fl(avius)... v(ir) c(larissimus) ... consularis\"?\n- The \"horreum\" and \"thermae\" don't have inscriptions.\n- There is a known Greek-Latin bilingual? Not sure.\n- The famous \"SEVERVS\" inscriptions? Not sure.\n\nI'm not confident on any specific epigraphic text from Mediana from memory. The safest well-known ones:\n- Naissus: the dedication to Jupiter by a beneficiarius? \n- The tombstone of a soldier of legio VII Claudia (which was stationed... no, VII Claudia was at Viminacium).\n\nHonestly — I should not list specific texts. I'll deliver:\n1. Access report (which tools failed, exactly how, with evidence).\n2. What each corpus is bibliographically (general, flagged as unverified-from-web).\n3. Concrete retrieval plan with exact URLs/parameters to use when access works (EDH API params, EDCS POST fields, bulk dumps).\n4. Explicit list of \"not verified\" items.\n\nBibliographic facts I can state with moderate confidence as general knowledge (clearly marked as \"po mojim dosadašnjim saznanjima, nije potvrđeno sa weba danas\"):\n- CIL III (1873, ed. Mommsen) — Naissus inscriptions in CIL III are few; the user's pointer \"CIL III p. 232, 1030; 8197ff\" matches the standard practice: CIL III p. 232 addenda and p. 1030 (index), and numbers 8197ff in the second supplement (CIL III Suppl. 2, published 1902) covering Upper Moesia.\n- IMS = \"Inscriptions de la Mésie Supérieure\" (Serbian: \"Inschriften aus Moesia Superior\"?) — series published in Belgrade by the Serbian Academy (SANU), Centre for... The series is commonly cited as IMS. Volumes:\n  - IMS I: Viminacium et Scupi (M. Mirković, Beograd 1979)? Hmm, I believe IMS I = \"Viminacium et Scupi\" is right? Or IMS I = \"Aquae\"? \n  Actually I recall: IMS I = Viminacium (Mirković 1979... no). Let me think about the well-known citation \"IMS VI, 68\" — hmm.\n  Known facts: IMS volumes published: I (Viminacium et Scupi, 1979), II (Margum, 1979?), III, IV, V (Aquae), VI (Scupi, 1983 - S. Dušanić?). \n  For Naissus specifically I have a vague memory that the Naissus volume is IMS VI? or that Naissus inscriptions are in IMS V/VI by P. Petrović. Petar Petrović published \"Inschriften aus Naissus\"? Hmm. Actually I do recall a volume: \"P. Petrović, Inscriptions de la Mésie Supérieure. IV. Naissus, Remesiana, Iusta... \" Not sure.\n  \n  There IS a well-known reference: \"IMS 6\" for Naissus? I've seen \"IMS VI 33\"? I can't verify.\n\nGiven the risk, I will clearly say: exact IMS volume/number assignment for Naissus NOT verified. And note that Naissus/Remesiana volume is often cited as IMS VI (uncertain) — hmm, better to say \"nije potvrđeno\".\n\nActually, I'm fairly confident about one thing: the Naissus epigraphic material was published in the IMS series by Petar Petrović, and there are about 70-80 inscriptions from Naissus. But number/volume uncertain.\n\nEDH: The API endpoint https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/data/api/search?find_location=Naissus is a real documented parameter (find_location). I can describe how to use it. Also EDH's Elites/geo JSON: https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/data/api/geo/search?searchstring=Naissus. And bulk CSV dumps exist. But Anubis blocks non-JS clients now.\n\nEDCS: manfredclauss.de search form is POST to https://manfredclauss.de/gb/search.php with fields like \"s_input\" ... I recall fields: search monuments by place uses field \"place_name\"? Not certain. I'll say it requires POST and can't be used via GET.\n\nAE: entries for Naissus/Mediana can't be verified.\n\nI also should mention the useful \"underway\" resource: the digital corpus \"EDH\" geo id for Naissus and the \"Trismegistos\" place ID for Naissus (TM Geo 33121?) — I guessed 33121 and never verified. Don't state it as fact; say ID unknown/unverified.\n\nAlso mention: \"Statuti\"? no.\n\nAlternative reliable route when access works:\n- EDH full-text search page: https://edh-www.adw.uni-heidelberg.de/inschrift/suche (POST/JS)\n- EDCS: https://manfredclauss.de/gb/search.php (POST; fields: hd_nr, place, etc.)\n- Last Statues of Antiquity: laststatues.info — search \"Mediana\" (has the \"horreum\"? no, has statue bases from Mediana villa with inscriptions).\n- Pleiades: pleiades.stoa.org/place/…Naissus\n- Trismegistos: trismegistos.org (TM Geo)\n- Corpus: \"Petar Petrović, Mediana:研究成果\"? The monograph: P. Petrović, \"Medijana\" (Niš 1995) — actually the well-known monograph is Petar Petrović, \"Mediana: резиденција римских царева...\"? I'll mention it cautiously.\n\nAlso I know the local repo has a geofizika_sloj.json etc. — not relevant.\n\nOne more consideration: maybe I should try the web_reader one final time right now before writing the report — it's been a few more minutes. Let me do exactly one call to a high-value URL (EDH geo search for Naissus, which would give the HD list). If it fails, finalize.\n\nLet me do that.","signature":"573bd889bd1b4d0eb49c5ee1"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_b0d4e2e5af4a4f86b1e2d808","session_id":"a06178bc-e4e6-4413-967f-cf91359c7b1b","uuid":"a880cb40-e83c-488d-8939-c5f7adee39e2","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:10:52.567Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"CIL III Naissus/Mediana korpus"}
