{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202610260614260ad1e76772ed4133","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_cb5a73afd5244de19d998ea1","content":"[{\"title\": \"Rhoimetalkes Mediana Asclepius at DuckDuckGo\", \"url\": \"https://html.duckduckgo.com/html/?q=Rhoimetalkes+Mediana+Asclepius\", \"content\": \"Rhoimetalkes Mediana Asclepius at DuckDuckGo\\n\\nAll Regions\\nArgentina\\nAustralia\\nAustria\\nBelgium (fr)\\nBelgium (nl)\\nBrazil\\nBulgaria\\nCanada (en)\\nCanada (fr)\\nCatalonia\\nChile\\nChina\\nColombia\\nCroatia\\nCzech Republic\\nDenmark\\nEstonia\\nFinland\\nFrance\\nGermany\\nGreece\\nHong Kong\\nHungary\\nIceland\\nIndia (en)\\nIndonesia (en)\\nIreland\\nIsrael (en)\\nItaly\\nJapan\\nKorea\\nLatvia\\nLithuania\\nMalaysia (en)\\nMexico\\nNetherlands\\nNew Zealand\\nNorway\\nPakistan (en)\\nPeru\\nPhilippines (en)\\nPoland\\nPortugal\\nRomania\\nRussia\\nSaudi Arabia\\nSingapore\\nSlovakia\\nSlovenia\\nSouth Africa\\nSpain (ca)\\nSpain (es)\\nSweden\\nSwitzerland (de)\\nSwitzerland (fr)\\nTaiwan\\nThailand (en)\\nTurkey\\nUS (English)\\nUS (Spanish)\\nUkraine\\nUnited Kingdom\\nVietnam (en)\\n\\nAny Time\\nPast Day\\nPast Week\\nPast Month\\nPast Year\\n\\n## Asclepius - Wikipedia\\n\\n![Image 1](https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/ip3/en.wikipedia.org.ico)\\nen.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asclepius\\n\\n__Asclepius__ (/ æsˈkliːpiəs /; Ancient Greek: Ἀσκληπιός Asklēpiós [asklɛːpiós]; Latin: Aesculapius) is a hero and god of medicine in ancient Greek religion and mythology. He is the son of Apollo and Coronis, or Arsinoe, or of Apollo alone. __Asclepius__ represents the healing aspect of the medical arts; his daughters, the Asclepiades, are: Hygieia (\\\"Health, Healthiness\\\"), Iaso ...\\n\\n## Rhoemetalces I - Wikipedia\\n\\n![Image 2](https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/ip3/en.wikipedia.org.ico)\\nen.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhoemetalces_I\\n\\nΑΕ 23.7, 11.1 g., struck 11 BC - 12 AD. The obverse shows the emperor Augustus, legend: ΚΑΙΣΑΡΟΣ ΣΕΒΑΣΤΟΥ; while the reverse shows Rhoemetalces I and his wife Pythodoris I, legend: ΒΑΣΙΛΕΩΣ ΡΟΙΜΗΤΑΛΚΟΥ. [1] Roman Province, Kingdom of Thrace, AE24, 10.1 g., struck 11 BC - 12 AD. Obverse: Jugate heads of Rhoemetalces I and his Queen Pythodoris I ...\\n\\n## Bosporos, Kings, Rhoemetalkes - Ancient Greek Coins - WildWinds.com\\n\\n![Image 3](https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/ip3/www.wildwinds.com.ico)\\nwww.wildwinds.com/coins/greece/bosporos/kings/rhoemetalkes/i.html\\n\\nAncient Coinage of Bosporos, Kings, Rhoemetalkes Browse the Rhoemetalkes page with thumbnail images. Note: For Rhoemetalkes with Augustus, see Thrace, Rhoemetalkes I.\\n\\n## CoinArchives.com Search Results : rhoemetalkes\\n\\n![Image 4](https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/ip3/www.coinarchives.com.ico)\\nwww.coinarchives.com/a/results.php?search=rhoemetalkes\\n\\nDiscover auction results for coins associated with Rhoemetalkes, featuring detailed descriptions and historical insights.\\n\\n## Full text of \\\"Asclepius. The Perfect Discourse Of Hermes Trismegistus ...\\n\\n![Image 5](https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/ip3/archive.org.ico)\\narchive.org/stream/asclepius.theperfectdiscourseofhermestrismegistustranslatedbyclementsalaman/Asclepius. The Perfect Discourse of Hermes Trismegistus translated by Clement Salaman_djvu.txt\\n\\nFull text of \\\"__Asclepius__. The Perfect Discourse Of Hermes Trismegistus Translated By Clement Salaman\\\" See other formats __ASCLEPIUS__ The Perfect D, iscourse of Hermes Trismegistus CLEMENT SALAMAN __Asclepius__ This page intentionally left blank __ASCLEPIUS__ The Perfect Discourse of Hermes Trismegistus edited and translated by Clement Salaman BLOOMS BURY LONDON • NEW DELHI • NEW YORK • SYDNEY ...\\n\\n## Apuleius and the \\\"Asclepius\\\" - JSTOR\\n\\n![Image 6](https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/ip3/www.jstor.org.ico)\\nwww.jstor.org/stable/1584081\\n\\nThe __Asclepius__ has been transmitted among the philosophical works of Apuleius. These include a speech on demonology, De deo Socratis; a summary of the life and the doctrines of Plato, De Platone et eius dogmate; and a translation of a Pseudo-Aristotelic cosmological treatise, De mundo.\\n\\n## CoinArchives.com Search Results : Rhoimetalkes\\n\\n![Image 7](https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/ip3/www.coinarchives.com.ico)\\nwww.coinarchives.com/a/results.php?search=Rhoimetalkes\\n\\nYour search for __'Rhoimetalkes'__ matched 10 lots from auctions added in the last six months. Only the first 100 results are shown. To search our full database of over 10 million records, please subscribe to CoinArchives Pro.\\n\\n## Thrace, Kings, Rhoemetalkes I - Ancient Greek Coins - Wildwinds\\n\\n![Image 8](https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/ip3/wildwinds.com.ico)\\nwildwinds.com/coins/greece/thrace/kings/rhoemetalkes_I/i.html\\n\\nAncient Coinage of Thrace, Kings, Rhoemetalkes I Browse the Rhoemetalkes I page with thumbnail images.\\n\\n## Fragment of a Statue of Asclepius from Mediana (2017).pdf\\n\\n![Image 9](https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/ip3/www.academia.edu.ico)\\nwww.academia.edu/35040097/Fragment_of_a_Statue_of_Asclepius_from_Mediana_2017_pdf\\n\\nThe head fragment likely represents __Asclepius__, dating from the 2nd to early 3rd century AD. The statue may have been brought to __Mediana__ during Emperor Julian's rule. The hair style indicates possible stylistic connections to both __Asclepius__ and Zeus. This work highlights the eclecticism in Roman sculpture influenced by Greek and Hellenistic styles. The cult of __Asclepius__ significantly flourished ...\\n\\n## Asklepieia: Healing Centers | Ασκληπιεία: Θεραπευτικά Κέντρα - Ancient ...\\n\\n![Image 10](https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/ip3/ancient-greece.org.ico)\\nancient-greece.org/history/asklepieia-healing-centers/\\n\\nThese sites became massive centers of learning and culture, often featuring theaters, gymnasia, and libraries alongside the traditional temple of __Asclepius__. The expansion of these sanctuaries allowed for a standardized approach to medicine that influenced the Galenic traditions of the Roman era.\\n\\nFeedback\\n\\n![Image 11](https://duckduckgo.com/t/sl_h)\", \"metadata\": {\"referrer\": \"origin\", \"viewport\": \"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=3.0, user-scalable=1\", \"HandheldFriendly\": \"true\", \"robots\": \"noindex, nofollow\"}, \"external\": {\"stylesheet\": {\"//duckduckgo.com/dist/h.12e359033b8c1146e5f7.css\": {\"media\": \"handheld, all\", \"type\": \"text/css\"}}, \"search\": {\"//duckduckgo.com/opensearch_html_v2.xml\": {\"title\": \"DuckDuckGo (HTML)\", \"type\": \"application/opensearchdescription+xml\"}}, \"shortcut\": {\"//duckduckgo.com/favicon.ico\": {}}, \"icon\": {\"//duckduckgo.com/favicon.ico\": {\"type\": \"image/x-icon\"}}, \"image_src\": {\"//duckduckgo.com/assets/icons/meta/DDG-icon_256x256.png\": {}}, \"apple-touch-icon\": {\"//duckduckgo.com/assets/icons/meta/DDG-iOS-icon_152x152.png?v=2\": {\"sizes\": \"152x152\"}, \"//duckduckgo.com/assets/icons/meta/DDG-iOS-icon_76x76.png?v=2\": {\"sizes\": \"76x76\"}, \"//duckduckgo.com/assets/icons/meta/DDG-iOS-icon_60x60.png?v=2\": {}, \"//duckduckgo.com/assets/icons/meta/DDG-iOS-icon_120x120.png?v=2\": {\"sizes\": \"120x120\"}}}}]"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_6ea3e54f733a4c3aa9de858d","session_id":"a06178bc-e4e6-4413-967f-cf91359c7b1b","uuid":"81467bb0-1594-4375-842b-45aea7861152","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:14:47.387Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Web research epigrafskih natpisa"}
