{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202610260641179c54c417559f4fc6","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The situation: I was working on the epigraphy task. Background agents fell with process tree at 23:23. I need to do the remaining work synchronously: Roimetalkos dedications, Dea Dardanica parallels, bronze railing. Skip LSA/bases that are stuck. Deliverable: nalaz.md and natpisi.json in this folder. If Write is refused, deliver both files inline in code-fence blocks.\n\nI have from local sources:\n1. **Ampelius inscription** (horreum): I(ovi) O(ptimo) M(aximo) / Co(ho)rtali / Aurel(ius) Ampelius trib(unus) Bat(avorum) + more lines ending \"que omnium votum posuerunt\" — ob dedicationem domus. Time of Constantine. tribunus Batavorum, imperial guard (auxilia palatina).\n2. **Fragmented inscription** in southern church (early christian church no. 1): \"domi[-nus]\" first line, \"providentiae\" second line — related to an emperor.\n3. **Deo Invicto** — two lines, from horreum (second found in horreum), Mithras or Sol.\n4. **Porphyry Asclepius** 43 cm, inv. 985/R — Greek: \"To Asclepius the Savior, Roimetalkes and his wife Philipa gratefully raise the monument.\" Room w-4, found 1971 (baza) / Hygeia found 1972 (Starinar 64/2014 footnote).\n5. **Porphyry Hygeia** 49 cm, inv. 986/R — Greek: \"To Hygeia, Roimetalkes, diasemotatos, and his wife Philipa grateful raise the monument.\"\n6. **Marble Asclepius with Telesphoros** 52 cm, inv. 987/R, 988/R, 988a/R — Greek: \"To Asclepius the Savior, Sim[...] a priest.\"\n7. **Dea Dardanica** — sculpture at entrance (~330); corpus: 8 stone monuments total — 5 votive with inscriptions (3 from Venden, 1 from Smira village, 1 from Kuršumlijska Banja), 2 votive plates from Romula-Malva in Dacia with relief + inscription, 1 sculpture from Mediana. Refs: E. Dobruna-Salihu, VAMZ 3/45, 2012, 218-219; I. Popović, Niš i Vizantija 6, 2008, 31-43.\n8. **Bronze railing** — cancelli with hermae (Asclepius, Luna busts; missing Hygeia, Sol); made before 325, installed 361 (Julian's stay), hidden 378. NO inscription mentioned in sources — the task asks \"šta je čitljivo\" — answer honestly: no inscriptions reported on the railing in available sources.\n9. **Frog pendant with Greek inscription ZO[HN] (life)** — black glass pendant, from Medijana (late antique finds, Gothic foederati context).\n10. Two altars with inscriptions from western section of horreum — dedicated to Jupiter and Mithras (secondary use as press counterweights). The Ampelius one is the Jupiter one; the Mithras one might be the Deo Invicto.\n\nNow I need to do web verification for:\n- Roimetalkos dedications: Greek text, IM numbers, CIL. Note: Ῥοιμέταλκος is a Thracian name (cf. Rhoemetalces, Thracian kings). \"diasemotatos\" = διασημότατος, a late Roman title.\n- CIL III 8197ff for Naissus. CIL III 8195-8218 are Naissus region. Ampelius inscription might be CIL III 8197? Let me verify via EDCS.\n- IM IV (Inscriptions de la Mésie Supérieure IV, Naissus, Remesiana, Iustyniana Prima, ed. P. Petrović, Beograd 1979) numbers.\n- Dea Dardanica today: Narodni muzej Niš? Let me search.\n- EDCS/EDH URLs.\n\nI should do this efficiently — synchronous web searches, then write the files. Let me start with WebSearch for the key items in parallel.\n\nNote: the \"pozadinska tri agenta\" mentioned — they fell; I shouldn't wait. Also \"LSA/baze koje su zaglavljene preskoci\" — skip those.\n\nLet me do web searches now. I'll batch a few.","signature":"b19d3e40ef0e4750ae32e1f4"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2e61857-1b3e-4231-a8c6-156332514500","uuid":"b64d650d-f20a-4672-8f57-14147d2141c5","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:41:38.758Z"}
