{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202610260642162db5c7926ab542b4","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Network access via curl is blocked by permissions too. So all web tools are unavailable in this session right now (WebSearch denied, WebFetch denied, webReader MCP erroring, curl requires approval).\n\nWait — maybe there are cached resources in the repo from earlier waves. The roj_glm folder has other workers' folders: objekti_CD has skinuto/*.txt files including aus2011.txt (Anteusage?), jeremic files, rai_783.html, rai_1184.html. Also `ap11_search.txt` and `ap11_zotovic.txt`. There's also `wd_claims.txt`, `osm_nominatim.json`. And the memory note says \"Jeremić 2006 tri URL-a\" was part of a pending task.\n\nThe user said: \"Ne ponavljaj vec uradjeno (LSA/baze koje su zaglavljene preskoci).\" — meaning skip stuck background work. And deliver synchronously with what I have. The user anticipated Write might be refused and asked for inline delivery in code fences.\n\nLet me check what network-derived material already exists locally in the roj folders that could help with epigraphy — particularly komparativni_korpus/nalaz.md, objekti_CD/skinuto files (aus2011.txt mentions Roimetalk? The grep earlier matched roj_glm files for my pattern). From the earlier grep results, files matching \"Roimetal|natpis|CIL|Dardanica\" in roj_glm:\n- roj_glm/komparativni_korpus/nalaz.md\n- roj_glm/komparativni_korpus/korpus.json\n- roj_glm/objekti_CD/skinuto/aus2015.txt ... aus2021.txt\n- roj_glm/objekti_CD/skinuto/jeremic_mozaici_2009.txt\n- roj_glm/objekti_CD/skinuto/jeremic_meduza_2017.txt\n- roj_glm/objekti_CD/rai_783.html, rai_1184.html\n\nLet me grep those for epigraphy content — especially Roimetalk, CIL, IM, Dardanica. This is local, allowed, and uses already-fetched material (dostupno odmah). Then I'll build the catalog from: (a) local monograph texts (primary), (b) cached web files if they contain epigraphic data.\n\nFor the Greek transcriptions: I know the standard formulas. I must be honest about confidence. The standard reconstruction:\n- Asclepius base: Ἀσκληπιῷ Σωτῆρι Ῥοιμέταλκος καὶ ἡ γυνὴ αὐτοῦ Φίληπ(π)α εὐχὴν (?) — but the monograph's English says \"gratefully raise the monument\" — likely \"εὐχαρίστως ἀνέστησαν\" or \"εὐχάριστος ἀνέστησεν\"... I should NOT fabricate a precise Greek text. I'll record the translation from the monograph (visoko poverenje) and mark the Greek reconstruction as hipotetična with nisko poverenje, clearly flagged as rekonstrukcija po formuli, ne očitano sa izvora. Actually better: put \"tekst\" as the English translation from monograph + formulaic Greek in brackets marked as rekonstrukcija. Honesty first.\n\nKnown epigraphic parallels for the name: Ῥοιμέταλκης (Rhoemetalces) — Thracian royal name (three Thracian kings Rhoemetalces I, II, III). The Mediana dedicant Ῥοιμέταλκος with title διασημότατος (diasemotatos — \"most distinguished\", late Roman rank below clarissimus, used for provincial elites). This suggests a Thracian-origin high official. Popović/Nikolić literature: \"Roimetalkes\" — I recall the name also appears in relation to a vila in the Balkans. I'll mark poreklo imena as tračansko (visoko-srednje: Rhoemetalces is attested as Thracian royal name; the form Ῥοιμέταλκος with -ος ending).\n\nFor CIL III 8197ff: Naissus inscriptions in CIL III are in the range 8195–8218 (CIL III 8197 = ?). I cannot verify exact numbers without web access. I must record honestly: CIL III brojevi za Naissus nisu verifikovani (mreža nedostupna), korpus je IM IV (Petrović 1979). The task says \"konflikti se upisuju\" and \"ograničenja upisati iskreno\" — so I'll be explicit: mrežni sloj (EDCS/EDH) nedostupan u ovoj sesiji (Write/WebSearch/WebFetch odbijeni; webReader mrežna greška), svi brojevi koji nisu iz lokalnih izvora označeni kao neverifikovani.\n\nWait — actually, let me double-check whether ap11_search.txt (37KB, from arheoloski pregled